<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Sandbox posture (contracts/downloads.md §3, spec FR-014, SC-010):
	     App Sandbox ON; user-selected read-write is the ONLY file
	     entitlement (the NSSavePanel Powerbox grant is the write
	     permission). Adding ANY further key is a recorded FR-014
	     deviation, never a silent edit. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- RECORDED FR-014 DEVIATION (T025 register item (a), 2026-07-17;
	     the internal macOS acceptance integration report):
	     macOS WebKit's out-of-process networking stack refuses to start
	     ANY navigation inside a sandboxed host without the outgoing-
	     connections entitlement — even for purely local custom-scheme
	     (app://local) content served by WKURLSchemeHandler from the app
	     process. Observed on the signed local build (macOS 26/Xcode 27):
	     webView.URL stays nil, isLoading stays false, white window; the
	     identical webview + handler wiring serves byte-complete content in
	     the unsigned (sandbox-unenforced) hosted test arm. The offline
	     claim therefore falls back to the runtime zero-non-app-origin-
	     request assertion (spec FR-014; the whole T026 acceptance session
	     runs with networking disabled), and the CI entitlements lint pins
	     THIS exact three-key posture. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
